# Implementation Plan: Remove Response Refiner & Polish Agent and Clean Greeting Agent Scope

This plan outlines the changes needed to remove the **Stage 3 — Response Refiner & Polish** agent across the entire query pipeline and update the **Greeting** agent so that it no longer references or lists out-of-scope categories.

---

## 1. Summary of Understanding

- **Response Refiner & Polish Agent**: Currently acts as an extra post-processing step (`_polish_answer`) invoked on responses from Conversational, Global Summary, and ServiceNow RAG flows. We will remove this agent entirely, returning raw/draft generation outputs directly to reduce latency, simplify token usage, and remove the refiner trace from the UI.
- **Greeting Agent & Out of Scope Categories**: Currently, the Greeting agent builds its prompt dynamically and mentions scope constraints / out-of-scope boundaries. We will clean up the Greeting agent to eliminate references to out-of-scope categories, providing a clean, welcoming greeting focused purely on ServiceNow assistance without reciting out-of-scope constraints.

---

## 2. User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> - **Latency Improvement**: Removing the Response Refiner agent will eliminate a secondary LLM round-trip on every answer, speeding up query response times significantly.
> - **Direct RAG Output**: The RAG and Conversational pipelines will directly output the primary model's generation without secondary formatting rewrites.

